mapspinner is SCALE-INVARIANT for small consumer planets (spoint): Quadtree(R) (planet-orchestrator passes the configured radius; was hardcoded 6360000 -> camAlt-negative broken LOD mesh at small radius), uReliefScale DECOUPLED from radius (gl-render setComposeHeightUniforms sets uReliefScale = g('reliefScale', opts.reliefScale ?? R/6360000) PER FRAME, so window.__reliefScale is LIVE; height-cpu.js mirrors reliefScale = opts.reliefScale ?? radius/6360000 in heightAt so CPU physics == GPU render), and the skirt floor scales with uReliefScale (terrain.glsl: max(tile*0.06, 30*uReliefScale); was absolute 30m -> deep skirt walls at small radius). spoint world def terrain has TWO independent knobs: radius (planet size/horizon, far ~ sqrt(R)) and reliefScale (relief/mountain height). Default reliefScale R/6360000 = unchanged pristine Earth look. ALL gl-render terrain knobs are live per-frame via window.__<name>: reliefScale, hiFreqCut, landBias, detailOverlay, canyonDepth, cliffAmt, beachShelf, octMax.